# ── Front-end (Vite, read at build time) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the state server is. Not needed when the server serves the built app itself (the hosted setup), nor under
# `npm run dev` on the default port 5173 (→ :3001). Set it for any other dev port, or a separately hosted server.
# VITE_QC_SERVER=https://qcteam-proto.onrender.com

# ── State server (server/server.mjs, read at start) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Access key every device enters once (Settings of the hosting service → Environment). Without it the API is OPEN to
# anyone who knows the URL — only acceptable on a laptop. Use 24+ random characters, e.g.:  openssl rand -base64 24
# QC_APP_TOKEN=

# Shared secret the Google Apps Script sends as X-Sync-Key on every push to /sheet/<purpose>. Required once
# QC_APP_TOKEN is set (the script has no cookie), otherwise pushes are refused with 401.
# QC_SYNC_KEY=

# Persistent disk for state.json, photos/ and backups/ (Render Disk → /data). Default: next to server.mjs.
# STATE_DIR=/data

# PORT is set by the host; defaults to 3001.
